winemac: Attach a replacement context to an established hidden GL client view.

After the upstream GDI client-view hide repair (1a1d1f3f), a new context on
that view can otherwise remain latent until viewWillDraw. Its first GL
commands then have no drawable; the first subsequent SwapBuffers reveals
old content. A previously used, realized, nonempty view can be attached
while hidden. Keep first-use, unrealized and zero-sized views deferred.

--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
@@ -602,7 +602,11 @@
         if (!pendingGlContexts)
             pendingGlContexts = [[NSMutableArray alloc] init];
 
-        if ([[self window] windowNumber] > 0 && !NSIsEmptyRect([self visibleRect]))
+        /* GDI can hide an established GL client view. Attach its replacement context
+           before the first GL commands, rather than waiting for a later viewWillDraw.
+           First-use, unrealized and zero-sized views must still remain deferred. */
+        if ([[self window] windowNumber] > 0 && (!NSIsEmptyRect([self visibleRect]) ||
+            (hadContext && [self isHidden] && !NSIsEmptyRect([self bounds]))))
         {
             [glContexts addObject:context];
             context.needsUpdate = TRUE;
